["haydock",2,null,"haydock","Blood. Why dost thou cease to admonish and rebuke the people? (Worthington) — Pronounce sentence on Jerusalem, (Haydock) for her cruelties. (Calmet)"],["haydock",6,null,"theodoret","Hath. Septuagint, “was mixed with his relations,” ver. 10., &c., (Haydock) fighting against them. (Theodoret)"],["haydock",8,null,"haydock","Sabbaths, by servile works, and by their sinful deportment."],["haydock",9,null,"haydock","Slanderers, hateful to all, Leviticus xix. 16., and Proverbs xi. 13. — Mountains. Chap. xviii. 6."],["haydock",10,null,"haydock","Father, his widow, their mother-in-law, or one of his wives."],["haydock",12,null,"jerome","Increase. Chap. xviii. 18. (Calmet) — Me. “The remembrance of God excludes all sins.” (St. Jerome)"],["haydock",13,null,"haydock","Hands, through surprise and sorrow. (Calmet) — God wishes the sinner’s salvation, Genesis vi. 6. (Worthington)"],["haydock",15,null,"haydock","In thee. I will purify thee by violent medicines. (Calmet)"],["haydock",16,null,"haydock","Possess, “as an inheritance:” (Septuagint; Haydock) “I will defile:” (Aquila) “wound thee.” (Symmachus) Hebrew is very different: (Calmet) “thou hast inherited in thyself,” (Haydock) being no longer willing to be subject."],["haydock",18,null,"haydock","Dross. Hebrew, “a mixture.” Septuagint, “God will purify the silver,” Isaias iv. 4."],["haydock",24,null,"haydock","Rained upon, or watered with the instructions of the prophets, chap. xx. 46."],["haydock",25,null,"haydock","Conspiracy. The false prophets defend each other, (Calmet) while the priests connive at their proceedings, (Haydock) and set the example of wickedness."],["haydock",28,null,"haydock","Without. Septuagint, “they shall fall, seeing,” &c."],["haydock",30,null,"haydock","None like Abraham, Moses, &c. (Calmet) — The prayers of the just are very powerful; and God wishes them to exert themselves for sinners. (St. Jerome) (Worthington)"]],"au":{"haydock":["George Leo Haydock",0,0,1849,"https://www.newadvent.org/cathen/07160a.htm"],"theodoret":["Theodoret of Cyrus",0,1,457,"https://www.newadvent.org/cathen/14570a.htm"],"jerome":["Jerome",1,1,420,"https://www.newadvent.org/fathers/#jerome"]}}